## Task type → routing rules

<!-- user-override -->
<!-- These are technology-neutral defaults. `/sdd:tasks` picks a task `type` from this table and
     `/sdd:implement` routes the task to the listed agent + skills, on the listed model tier.
     Add stack-specific types (and their agents/skills/model) below or in "Custom routing rules".

     Stack = which projects a row applies to: `*` for any, a project name (`api`), its kind
     (`mobile`) or a stack word from the Projects list (`python`, `nextjs`, `flutter`). The most
     specific match wins (project name, then kind/stack word, then `*`), so one task type can route
     to a different specialist per project. Route only to agents that can edit files (their tools
     include Write/Edit) — a read-only agent (an architect, a reviewer) cannot implement a task.
     One without Bash is fine: /sdd:implement runs its tests for it.

     Model = the cost tier of the subagent that runs the task: /sdd:implement passes it as the
     subagent's `model` (for a task done inline it only advises the session model, which a command
     cannot switch). Reserve `opus` for judgement-heavy REASONING phases run at the session level
     (/sdd:spec, /sdd:clarify, /sdd:plan, /sdd:review); keep the mechanical implement-phase task
     tiers cheap. `haiku` for trivial/mechanical work, `sonnet` for
     normal test + implementation work. -->
| Task type           | Stack | Specialist agent          | Skills to load                          | Model   |
|---------------------|-------|---------------------------|-----------------------------------------|---------|
| contract            | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | sonnet  |
| implementation      | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | sonnet  |
| integration-test    | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | sonnet  |
| e2e-test            | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | sonnet  |
| migration           | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | sonnet  |
| refactor            | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | haiku   |
| generic             | *     | (orchestrator)            | —                                       | haiku   |

